cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Anomaly Detection in EV Battery Charging: LSTM-based State-of-Charge
  Estimation and Sensor-Fault Detection
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Farhad
    family-names: Bagheri
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/FarhadBagheri23/Anomaly-Detection-SoC-EV-batteries
abstract: >-
  A battery management system reports State of Charge but cannot measure it
  directly; it infers SoC by integrating current, so any current-sensor error
  accumulates rather than averaging away. This work trains an LSTM-family
  estimator on the LG 18650HG2 benchmark across -20 to +40 degrees C and uses
  its prediction as an independent second opinion, monitoring the residual
  between reported and predicted SoC increments to detect bias, drift and
  noise faults in the measurement chain.
keywords:
  - state of charge
  - lithium-ion battery
  - anomaly detection
  - LSTM
  - battery management system
  - electric vehicles
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-08-02'
